Harry Emerson Fosdick's pastorate at the Riverside Church in Morningside Heights, Manhattan, was a significant event in the history of American Protestantism. He became a central figure in the "Fundamentalist–Modernist Controversy" within American Protestantism in the 1920s and 1930s. This controversy was sparked by his sermon "Shall the Fundamentalists Win?" in 1922, which challenged traditional Christian doctrines and ignited a debate between fundamentalists and modernists.
