What is the historical context surrounding the resignation of the Austrian Empire's Foreign Minister?
The historical context surrounding the resignation of the Austrian Empire's Foreign Minister, Klemens von Metternich, is the liberal Revolutions of 1848. The economic crisis of 1845-47 led to recession and food shortages, and the February victories in Paris prompted uprisings throughout Europe, including in Vienna. The Diet of Lower Austria demanded Metternich's resignation in March, and with no forces rallying to his defense, he resigned on March 13, 1848.
