What was the name of the 1994 Formula One season race where Roland Ratzenberger was killed, and what was the significance of this event in relation to the 1994 Monaco Grand Prix?
The 1994 Formula One season race where Roland Ratzenberger was killed was the 1994 San Marino Grand Prix. This event was significant because it occurred two weeks before the 1994 Monaco Grand Prix, and the deaths of Ratzenberger and Ayrton Senna at the San Marino Grand Prix led to a somber atmosphere and a tribute to the deceased drivers at the Monaco Grand Prix, which included a "missing man formation" during the race.
